where e denotes the final object of H\unsure{o}t , and is used for defining the
pointed structure of the second member. The functor $\overset{\hand{\sim}}{W}$ in (8) can be
described (as is seen componentwise) as

(11) \qquad $\overset{\hand{\sim}}{W}\ (X_*) = W(\hand{\beta}(X_*))/ \mathrm{Im}\, W(e_*)$ \quad ,

where
\[ W(e_*) \longrightarrow W(X_*) \qquad \text{i.e.} \qquad \underline{Z}^{(e\ )} \longrightarrow \underline{Z}^{(X\ )} \]
is deduced from the pointing map $e_* \longrightarrow X_*$ . Accordingly we get
an expression

\xout{(12)} \qquad $\overset{\hand{\sim}}{\mathrm{LH}}_{\hand{\bullet}}(X) \hand{\simeq} \mathrm{LH}_{\hand{\bullet}}(X)/\mathrm{LH}_{\hand{\bullet}}(e)$ \qquad ,

